//? Title: Historical RC4: actual KSA swaps, PRGA bytes and a deterministic bias study
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A stream cipher combines plaintext with a generated byte stream, so repeating a
stream repeats its mask. Historical RC4 builds that stream from a256-byte
permutation; its known biases make it unsuitable for modern secure protocols.
This report reads actual native schedule/swap/output decisions, retains the
original ciphertext vectors and 20,000-key experiment, and correctly labels that
key sequence as deterministic rather than random independent draws.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

KSA starts from the identity permutation, updating j by the current permutation
entry and a key byte before swapping. PRGA then updates i and j, swaps S[i] and
S[j], and reads
$$ K=S[(S[i]+S[j])\bmod256],\qquad C=P\mathbin\oplus K. $$
\alttext(The actual post-swap permutation lookup supplies one byte XORed with the plaintext.)
Every swap preserves the permutation invariant. XORing the same keystream twice
restores the input, explaining round-trip behavior but providing no
authentication or key-reuse protection. The native step record comes from the
same update used by next(), not a state replay. KSA costs 256 swaps per fresh
key and PRGA constant work per byte.

Published RC4 second-byte biases concern a key distribution and cryptanalytic
setting. The original experiment instead generates formatted decimal strings
with a wrapping integer recipe. Its exact second-byte and grouped histograms are
finite outcomes of that recipe; distinct-key counts expose repetitions and do
not make the observations iid.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/rc4_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/modular_exponentiation.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/integer_arithmetic.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <climits>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/number_theory.hpp>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/prufer.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/flow_diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/geometry/hull_algorithms.hpp>
#include <datamunge/random/sampling_analysis.hpp>
#include <iomanip>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/qr_algorithm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/stats/lm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/arithmetic_coding.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/rbf.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/model_plot.hpp>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/rc4.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    auto t = a::rc4_trace("Key", 3);
    const auto &k = t.scheduling[0];
    const auto &s = t.steps[0];
    std::print("\n| actual PRGA byte | i before | j before | i after | j after | actual output index | " "emitted byte |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        const auto &e = t.steps[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:02x} |\n", i,
                   unsigned(e.i_before), unsigned(e.j_before),
                   unsigned(e.i_after), unsigned(e.j_after),
                   unsigned(e.output_index), unsigned(e.output));
    }

    g::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first KSA index / updated j\n{} / {}", k.i,
                       unsigned(k.j_after)));
    d.node("n1", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual first PRGA i / j\n{} / {}", unsigned(s.i_after),
                       unsigned(s.j_after)));
    d.node("n2", {20, 0},
           std::format("Actual emitted first byte\n{:02x}", unsigned(s.output)));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/rc4_tiny.svg");
}
```
